# LeakSanitizer suppressions for tools/sanitizers/run.sh asan (Linux only:
# LSan is not supported on macOS). Format: one `leak:<pattern>` per entry,
# each directly preceded by a comment block containing `# why: <reason>`
# that names the code covered and why the report is a false positive or out
# of our control. Never this workspace's own crates or the C++ shim: those
# reports are bugs. tools/sanitizers/check-suppressions.sh enforces all this.
